# Repo selection scopes the entire workspace below the header

id: desktop-repo-workspace
version: 1
status: proposed
title: Top bar repo dropdown drives workspace scope

goal: >
  One active repo at a time. The dropdown in the persistent header is the
  primary control for which repository the agent workspace, session list, and
  connection context use.

state:
  source: desktopState
  fields:
    - repoPath
    - repos
    - landingRepoPath

controls:
  - id: repo_dropdown
    location: top_bar
    placement: immediately_right_of_sidebar_toggle
    type: custom_combobox_or_select
    display:
      - repo_name
      - optional_path_truncation
    actions:
      - select_repo
      - add_repository
      - remove_repository_from_index

flows:
  - name: switch_active_repo
    trigger: user_selects_different_repo_in_dropdown
    steps:
      - set desktopState.repoPath to selected path
      - refresh session list for that repo in sidebar
      - if selectedSession belongs to other repo:
          clear or prompt to switch session
      - navigate to /workspace if on landing with repo chosen
      - optional: auto_connect per desktopSettings.autoConnectOnLaunch
    outcome: main_inset shows workspace for new repo; sidebar lists only that repo sessions

  - name: add_repo
    trigger: user_chooses_add_in_dropdown
    steps:
      - native folder picker via desktop shell API
      - index repo in SQLite metadata
      - append to repos list
      - set as active repo
    outcome: dropdown shows new repo; sidebar loads sessions

  - name: first_launch_no_repos
    trigger: repos empty
    steps:
      - show empty state in dropdown placeholder
      - sidebar shows add repo CTA or mirrors dropdown add action
      - workspace shows SessionLanding or empty workspace prompt
    outcome: user adds repo from dropdown before sessions appear

ui_rules:
  - Dropdown width capped; long paths in title attribute only
  - Active repo visually distinct in closed state (name + mono path chip optional)
  - Switching repo does not collapse session sidebar unless user toggled it

persistence:
  - remember last_active_repo_path in preferences
  - sidebarOpen unchanged on repo switch

acceptance:
  - Single repo dropdown is sufficient to change workspace without opening sidebar
  - Session sidebar always reflects active repo only (no multi-repo tree in sidebar)

open_questions:
  - id: recent_repos_section
    question: Pin recent repos in dropdown footer vs flat list?
  - id: worktree_display
    question: Show worktree path in dropdown when session uses worktree?
